   "id": "09.1",
   "movement": "THE SHARED MOON",
   "seconds": 17,
   "lines": "accepting you'll never / say nor / ever feel / my love was real— / what isn't mine, / I still can not give. / I gather my things to go. / before I go— / we look at the moon— / the way we used to see it / & settle down the stoicism. / we talk for years / & travel through time / & it feels so good— / we grow old together / I believe, maybe / we could have it all— / swinging my humbled / late nights & / heartbreaks at / an end story / unchanging.",
